            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0182" n="66" xml:id="pg66"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.9311/131.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chinese Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 14, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am instructed by my Government to inform
                    you that the Emperor of China, by a decree dated the 12th of February, has
                    formally abdicated the throne, and vested his excellency Yuan Shih Kai with full
                    power to adopt and establish a republican form of government; and that pending
                    the establishment of such a government the diplomatic and consular officers of
                    China abroad are to continue in the discharge of their respective functions as
                    representatives of China without interruption.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chang Yin Tang.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
